      <Row>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Enable interrupt on falling edge (neie)</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">test_gpio_nedge_random_pads_en</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Configure GPIO pads 8–39 for input mode with falling-edge interrupt; route the GPIO interrupt to the processor; randomly enable each pad once and drive a falling-edge stimulus via memory-mapped stimulus; verify the pin input state and group/raw interrupt status; then clear per-pin and group interrupt status and confirm system-level interrupt status is cleared.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The test enables the platform interrupt for GPIO instance (IRQ 87 for GPIO0 or 88 for GPIO1) and routes the corresponding GPIO interrupt in the system register. It initializes a random generator and uses a memory-mapped location (0xA0243ffc) to produce a stimulus pattern. In a loop, it selects a unique pad index 0..31 (mapping to GPIO pads 8..39), configures the per-pin control register (base GPIO_8 plus pad offset times four) to input with negedge interrupt (0x00140000), enables the group interrupt bit for that pad in INTR1_INTR_EN1, drives a negedge event by writing complement of a one shifted by pad index then all-ones to 0xA0243ffc, and waits for the interrupt by polling int_pend cleared in the ISR. The ISR reads the per-pin register to check DIN and raw-interrupt indications, verifies the group masked interrupt status in INTR1_INTR_STS1 for the same pad, disables group enables, clears the per-pin raw interrupt by writing 0x00110001 to the pin control register, confirms the per-pin register reflects the cleared value, ensures the group status clears to 0x0, and finally clears/validates the system raw interrupt status for the respective instance. Any mismatch increments test_err; finish(test_err) reports the result.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">ISR</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xA0243ffc</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xA0243ffc</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Random unique selection covers pads 8–39 exactly once; requires routing of GPIO interrupt to the processor through INTR_EN1; group interrupt enable and status must be managed per selected pad via INTR1_INTR_EN1 and INTR1_INTR_STS1; uses IRQ 87 (GPIO0) or IRQ 88 (GPIO1); stimulus is driven via memory-mapped address 0xA0243ffc.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1) Enable processor IRQ for the GPIO instance and route the GPIO interrupt in INTR_EN1. 2) Initialize stimulus by writing all-ones to 0xA0243ffc. 3) For each pad 8–39, select a new random pad. 4) Configure the selected pad for input with falling-edge interrupt. 5) Enable the selected pad’s group interrupt bit in INTR1_INTR_EN1. 6) Drive a falling-edge stimulus for the selected pad, then restore all-ones. 7) Wait for the ISR to run. 8) In ISR, verify per-pin DIN and raw interrupt, and confirm group status. 9) Clear per-pin interrupt and confirm per-pin and group status clear. 10) Clear system raw interrupt status and confirm clear. 11) Repeat for all pads and report result.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Setup: conditionally enable IRQ 87 or 88. Route interrupt via INTR_EN1. Seed RNG. Initialize stimulus to all-ones at 0xA0243ffc. Loop for 32 iterations enforcing unique selection. For each chosen pad: program per-pin control to 0x00140000; wait; set INTR1_INTR_EN1 bit for pad; write complement of one shifted by pad index to 0xA0243ffc then restore; set int_pend and wait until ISR clears it. ISR: clear int_pend; read per-pin register; check DIN bit equals expected state; check raw interrupt bit set; read INTR1_INTR_STS1 and check selected pad bit set; mask group enables; write 0x00110001 to per-pin control and verify readback 0x00100001; verify INTR1_INTR_STS1 reads zero; clear system raw interrupt for instance and verify cleared; clear GIC IRQ.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO_8 (per-pin control, pad offset 0..31), INTR1_INTR_EN1 (group interrupt enable), INTR1_INTR_STS1 (group interrupt status), INTR_EN1 (system interrupt enable routing), gpio_intr_raw_stclr1 (system raw interrupt status/clear)</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For each selected pad, a falling-edge stimulus triggers an interrupt; the pin input state indicates the expected active state; INTR1_INTR_STS1 shows the pad bit set; after clearing per-pin and group status, INTR1_INTR_STS1 reads 0; the system raw interrupt status is cleared; overall test passes with zero errors.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">DIN check: per-pin read bit0 nonzero expected; raw interrupt asserted: per-pin read bit1 nonzero; group status asserted: INTR1_INTR_STS1 has selected pad bit set; after clear sequence per-pin read equals 0x00100001 and group status equals 0; system raw cleared after write to instance bit; if no interrupt path taken, count error.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">#include&lt;lss_sysreg.h&gt;, #include&lt;stdlib.h&gt;, #include&lt;stdio.h&gt;, #include&lt;test_define.c&gt;, #include&lt;test_common.h&gt;, #include&lt;time.h&gt;, #include&lt;gpio/gpio_def.h&gt;, #include&lt;gpio/gpio_offset.h&gt;</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">#define CNT 49</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">addr_array[49] (GPIO_8..GPIO_39, GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, INTR1/2 EN1 &amp; STS1, IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4, DOUT/DIN_GROUP1..4); default_value_array[49]; read_mask_array[49]; write_mask_array[49]; skip_array[49] all zeros</Data></Cell>
      </Row>
      <Row>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Enable interrupt on falling edge (neie)</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">test_gpio_nedge_walking_zeros_pattern</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Configure GPIO pads 8–39 for input with falling-edge interrupt and appropriate I/O control; enable all group interrupts; sequentially drive a walking-zeros falling-edge pattern per pad via memory-mapped stimulus; verify pin input and group/raw interrupt status; then clear per-pin and group interrupt status and confirm system-level interrupt status is cleared.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The test enables the platform interrupt for the GPIO instance and routes it in the system register. It programs per-pin negedge interrupt enable for pads 8–39, configures I/O control groups, and enables all bits in INTR1_INTR_EN1. It iterates i from 0 to 31: writes all-ones to 0xA0243ffc, then writes complement of a one shifted by i to create a falling edge on pad 8+i; waits for ISR. The ISR clears int_pend, restores 0xffffffff to the stimulus, reads the per-pin register to validate DIN and raw interrupt bits, checks INTR1_INTR_STS1 for the pad bit, clears the per-pin interrupt by writing 0x00110001 and verifies readback 0x00100001, ensures INTR1_INTR_STS1 clears to zero, and clears/validates the system raw interrupt status.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">ISR</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xA0243ffc</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xA0243ffc</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sequential walking-zeros pattern across pads 8–39; requires system routing via INTR_EN1; group interrupt enable and status managed via INTR1_INTR_EN1 and INTR1_INTR_STS1; uses IRQ 87 or 88 depending on instance.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1) Enable processor IRQ and route GPIO interrupt via INTR_EN1. 2) Program per-pin falling-edge interrupt for pads 8–39. 3) Configure I/O control groups for pads 8–39. 4) Enable all group interrupts in INTR1_INTR_EN1. 5) For each pad, drive a falling-edge stimulus then restore. 6) Wait for ISR and verify per-pin DIN and raw interrupt, and group status. 7) Clear per-pin interrupt, confirm per-pin and group status clear. 8) Clear system raw interrupt status. 9) Repeat for all pads; report result.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Setup and route interrupts; for i from 0 to 31: write per-pin control 0x00040000; program IO control groups (IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4) to 0x000000FF; enable INTR1_INTR_EN1 to all ones; for each i compute one shifted by i, write all-ones to 0xA0243ffc, then complement of the shifted one; wait until ISR clears int_pend. ISR: restore 0xffffffff; read per-pin register; validate DIN bit and raw interrupt bit; read INTR1_INTR_STS1 and check bit i; write 0x00110001 to per-pin register and verify 0x00100001; confirm INTR1_INTR_STS1 equals zero; clear instance system raw status and verify; clear GIC IRQ.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO_8 (per-pin control), GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, gpio_io_ctrl_group4, INTR1_INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_STS1, INTR_EN1, gpio_intr_raw_stclr1</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each pad’s falling-edge transition triggers an interrupt; per-pin DIN and raw interrupt bits indicate the event; INTR1_INTR_STS1 shows the corresponding pad bit set; after clear operations, INTR1_INTR_STS1 reads zero and system raw interrupt is cleared; overall test passes with zero errors.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Per-pin read bit0 nonzero; per-pin raw interrupt bit1 set; group status has bit i set; after per-pin clear and waits, per-pin read equals 0x00100001; group status equals zero; system raw cleared after write to RAW_STCR1 for the instance; missing interrupt counts as error.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">#include&lt;lss_sysreg.h&gt;, #include&lt;stdio.h&gt;, #include&lt;test_define.c&gt;, #include&lt;test_common.h&gt;, #include&lt;gpio/gpio_def.h&gt;, #include&lt;gpio/gpio_offset.h&gt;</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">#define CNT 49</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">addr_array[49]; default_value_array[49]; read_mask_array[49]; write_mask_array[49]; skip_array[49] all zeros</Data></Cell>
      </Row>
      <Row>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Enable interrupt on falling edge (neie)</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">test_gpio_negedge_intr_en</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Configure GPIO pads 8–39 one by one for input with falling-edge interrupt; enable the group interrupt only for the active pad; drive a falling-edge stimulus per pad via memory-mapped stimulus; verify per-pin input and group/raw interrupt status; then clear per-pin and confirm group/system interrupt status clear.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The test enables and routes the GPIO interrupt in the system register. For each i in 0..31: it programs the per-pin control for pad 8+i to input with negedge enable (0x00140000), enables the corresponding bit in INTR1_INTR_EN1, writes all-ones then complement of a one shifted by i to 0xA0243ffc to generate a falling edge, and waits for ISR by polling int_pend. The ISR restores the stimulus to 0xffffffff, reads the per-pin register to check DIN and raw interrupt bits, checks INTR1_INTR_STS1 masked status for the same bit, clears the per-pin interrupt by writing 0x00110001 and verifies readback 0x00100001, confirms group status clears to zero, and clears the system raw interrupt for the instance.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">ISR</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xA0243ffc</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xA0243ffc</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sequential per-pad configuration and verification using routed interrupts; relies on INTR1_INTR_EN1 bit gating; uses IRQ 87 or 88 depending on instance; stimulus via 0xA0243ffc.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1) Enable and route GPIO interrupt via INTR_EN1. 2) For each pad 8–39: configure input with falling-edge enable. 3) Enable the pad’s group interrupt in INTR1_INTR_EN1. 4) Drive falling-edge stimulus for the pad, then restore; wait for ISR. 5) In ISR, verify per-pin DIN and raw interrupt, and group status. 6) Clear per-pin interrupt and confirm per-pin and group status clear. 7) Clear system raw interrupt for the instance. 8) Repeat for all pads; report result.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Enable system interrupt; loop over pads: write per-pin 0x00140000; wait; compute one shifted by i; enable INTR1_INTR_EN1 for that bit; write 0xA0243ffc to all-ones then complement to create negedge; set int_pend and wait until ISR clears it. ISR: restore 0xffffffff; read per-pin; validate DIN and raw interrupt; read INTR1_INTR_STS1 and check bit; write 0x00110001 and verify 0x00100001; confirm group status cleared; clear RAW_STCR1 for instance; clear GIC IRQ.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO_8 (per-pin control), INTR1_INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_STS1, INTR_EN1, gpio_intr_raw_stclr1</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each pad’s falling-edge transition triggers an interrupt; per-pin DIN and raw bits indicate the event; masked group status is set for the pad; after clear, per-pin readback and group status indicate cleared; system raw interrupt cleared; pass if no errors.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">DIN bit nonzero; raw interrupt bit set; group status contains active bit; after clear sequence, per-pin equals 0x00100001 and group status equals zero; RAW_STCR1 instance bit cleared; if no interrupt, error.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">#include&lt;stdio.h&gt;, #include&lt;lss_sysreg.h&gt;, #include "test_define.c", #include&lt;test_common.h&gt;, #include&lt;gpio/gpio_def.h&gt;, #include&lt;gpio/gpio_offset.h&gt;</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">#define CNT 49</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">addr_array[49]; default_value_array[49]; read_mask_array[49]; write_mask_array[49]; skip_array[49] all zeros</Data></Cell>
      </Row>
      <Row>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">dout</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">test_gpio_op_mode_all_pad_en</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Configure GPIO pads 8–39 for output mode using group I/O control; for each pad, drive output high then low via the per-pad control register and verify pad readback through the memory-mapped status reflects the driven value.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The test enables IRQs but does not use interrupts. It configures GPIO I/O control groups 1..4 with value 0x00FF00FF to set pads 8–39 to output mode. It enables group interrupt mask but does not rely on it. For each pad i in 0..31, it writes 0x00200000 to the per-pin control (drive high) and sets a flag to check, reads the memory-mapped pad status at 0xA0243ffc and verifies the corresponding bit is one, then writes 0x00000000 (drive low), reads back and verifies the bit is zero. Any mismatch increments test_err; finish(test_err) reports the result.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Polling</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xA0243ffc</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0xA0243ffc</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Validates per-pin output drive against pad readback; requires I/O control groups configured for output; uses per-pin control writes only; no ISR is expected.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1) Configure I/O control groups to output for pads 8–39. 2) Optionally enable group interrupts (not used). 3) For each pad, drive output high and verify pad readback shows one. 4) Drive output low and verify pad readback shows zero. 5) Repeat for all pads; report result.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Write IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4 to output; for each pad i: write per-pin control 0x00200000 then read 0xA0243ffc and verify bit i equals one; then write 0x00000000 and verify bit i equals zero; clear GIC IRQs if set spuriously.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO_8 (per-pin control), GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, gpio_io_ctrl_group4, INTR1_INTR_EN1</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For each pad, setting output high must reflect as a one in the pad readback; setting output low must reflect as a zero; overall pass if no mismatches are detected.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pad readback via 0xA0243ffc &amp; (one shifted by pad index) nonzero when driven high; equals zero when driven low; any deviation increments error count.</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">#include&lt;lss_sysreg.h&gt;, #include&lt;stdio.h&gt;, #include&lt;test_define.c&gt;, #include&lt;test_common.h&gt;, #include&lt;gpio/gpio_def.h&gt;, #include&lt;gpio/gpio_offset.h&gt;</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">#define CNT 49</Data></Cell>
        <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">addr_array[49]; default_value_array[49]; read_mask_array[49]; write_mask_array[49]; skip_array[49] all zeros</Data></Cell>
      </Row>
    </Table>
  </Worksheet>
</Workbook>